                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "content": "The top-rated car rental companies in London and Paris are Sixt and Europcar. The best-rated restaurants in London and Paris are Le Grand Vefour and Le Jules Verne. The most expensive hotels in London and Paris are The Ritz London and Shangri-La Hotel, Paris. \n\nThe total maximum expense for the 5-day trip, assuming 2 meals per day, can be calculated by adding the cost of the hotels and the cost of the meals. \n\nLet's assume the cost of the hotels is 1000 euros per night, and the cost of the meals is 50 euros per meal. \n\nThe total cost of the hotels for the 5-day trip would be: \n2 nights in London: 2 x 1000 = 2000 euros\n3 nights in Paris: 3 x 1000 = 3000 euros\nTotal cost of hotels: 2000 + 3000 = 5000 euros\n\nThe total cost of the meals for the 5-day trip would be: \n2 meals per day for 5 days: 2 x 5 = 10 meals\n10 meals x 50 euros per meal: 10 x 50 = 500 euros\n\nThe total maximum expense for the 5-day trip would be: \n5000 euros (hotels) + 500 euros (meals) = 5500 euros\n\nSo, the total maximum expense for the 5-day trip, assuming 2 meals per day, would be 5500 euros."
